# pcrec VM program listing (DD-8; docs/design/engine_m4.md S10)
#
# Produced BY the emitter's own walk, not by a second walk over the
# AST: every row below was written by the same call that wrote the
# corresponding C. S10's one constraint -- "the dump must be derived
# from the same structure the emitter walks, never a parallel
# description" -- is therefore structural here, not a discipline.
#
# TAB-separated, one #section per table, each with its own #header of
# column names: docs/spec/ir_listing.md is this listing's contract and
# docs/spec/table_contract.md is the TSV contract it conforms to.
# Resolve a column BY NAME; column WIDTH is not a contract. A DEBUG
# listing: complete for control structure, lossy on operands (D106).

#section summary
#fact	value	note
pattern	(ab){2,3}c	
engine	vm	forced by: capture group at pattern offset 0
prefilter	no-engine-vm	--engine=vm -- the VM scans from search_from itself (R21 E-6)
rungs	cursor	comma-joined; the rungs section below says which quantifier took which
strategies	possessive	comma-joined; the strategies section below says which quantifier took which
possessify	1/1	marked/total SOURCE quantifiers possessified (eng_brep_design.md S2)
caps	2	RX_NCAPS; 1 capturing group in the pattern text
step-budget	500000000	backtrack resumptions
resume-frames	1	
trail-entries	3	
subject-ceiling		exact: no subject ceiling
labels	3	
events	15	
resume-points	0	the PRE-PASS count the resume-point cap is checked against, never a recount of the event stream
max-replicas	0	limit 64, checked before emission
prune-ceiling	subject-end	the subject end -- either no prefilter, or the prefilter's window END is not a bound on this match's end: the pattern carries an ATOMIC GROUP (atomic_groups_design.md 4.4 H3) or a LOOKAROUND (lookaround_design.md 5.6), or the prefilter was built from the COUNT-COLLAPSED superset (prefilter_count_independence.md 2 H3, K39/[OPT-4]) -- the prefilter row above says which
prune-bound-sites	1	
prune-retreats	0	
islands	0	
callout-sites	0	

#section slots
#family	slot	holds	note
group	0,1	$0 whole match	written by the ENTRY, not the VM (S3.4)
group	2,3	group 1	written on traverse, trailed
guard			no empty-iteration guard slots: no nullable unbounded quantifier on the frames rung
low			no span-loop low-water slots: no cursor rung in this program
mark			
revdet			
lookmark			
lookpos			

#section rungs
#label	kind	detail
L0	cursor	span-loop cursor {2,3}, stride 2, greedy, POSSESSIFIED (no frame, no giveback)

#section strategies
#label	kind	detail
L0	possessive	span-loop cursor {2,3}, stride 2, greedy, POSSESSIFIED (no frame, no giveback)

#section pruning
#label	kind	detail
L0	clamped	span-loop cursor {2,3}, stride 2, greedy, POSSESSIFIED (no frame, no giveback)

#section program
#label	op	args	target	note
L0	label			span-loop cursor {2,3}, stride 2, greedy, POSSESSIFIED (no frame, no giveback)
	note			work charge: frameless scan iterations
	note			fewer than rmin iterations: the loop cannot be satisfied
	note			MRL: too few bytes remain after the loop's one exit position for any accepting continuation
	set	slot_values[2] <- scan_position		group 1 open, derived from the cursor
	set	slot_values[3] <- scan_position		group 1 close, derived from the cursor
	goto		L2	
L2	label			
	consume	'c'	L1	
	fail			backtrack
L1	label			the pattern is complete
	accept			
accept	label			return scan_position - ctx->pos; the capture slots at this instant ARE the answer (S3.1)
fail	label			the ONLY backtracker and the only indirect jump; one step charged here (S4.2)

#section choicepoints
#label	resume	note
		none: this program never backtracks -- it is a straight line, and the resume stack is never pushed. PREFERENCE ORDER: the frame pushed at a site resumes the LESS preferred alternative

#section islands
#label	width	note
		none: no flat alternation in this program has a finite literal language, so src/gen/emit_vm.c's alternation island declined every one -- docs/spec/tuning.md S2.20

#section callouts
#label	note
	none: module 'callouts' has no producer, so no pattern can reach a call site -- engine_m4.md S9.1
